local-07 (budi, 2026-10-12): staged prefill launch config for sm_86.

Idea from flash-next-qsa-fun-stages.patch (~/patch-qfn3), which exposed the
staged kernel's num_warps/num_stages as env variables. On sm_86 the default
table gives a staged prefill chunk (256-512 rows x 2 KV heads) BLOCK_N 64,
2 warps, 2 stages. Kernel sweep on an RTX 3060 (sm_86, FP8 cache, top-k 2048,
~98K context, BLOCK_N {32,64,128} x warps {1,2,4,8} x stages {1..4}): BLOCK_N 32
with 4 warps is 2.1-2.5x faster (512 rows, 1 bucket 15.0 -> 6.3 ms; 3 buckets
36.7 -> 14.7 ms; 256 rows 8.2 -> 3.9 ms); stages barely matter; BLOCK_N 128
does not fit sm_86 shared memory. Same accuracy vs an fp64 reference (rel L2
2.65e-3); max |diff| vs the default 3.9e-3 (BF16 rounding).

Only the staged kernel on compute capability 8.6 changes. Env:
  VLLM_QSA_STAGED_TUNE=0         default config again
  VLLM_QSA_STAGED_BLOCK_N/WARPS/STAGES   override one value (32 / 4 / 3)

diff --git a/vllm/models/qwen4_exp/nvidia/ops/qsa.py b/vllm/models/qwen4_exp/nvidia/ops/qsa.py
index f7f78ca..d7cd88e 100644
--- a/vllm/models/qwen4_exp/nvidia/ops/qsa.py
+++ b/vllm/models/qwen4_exp/nvidia/ops/qsa.py
@@ -28,6 +28,29 @@ def _is_sm90() -> bool:
     return current_platform.get_device_capability() == (9, 0)
 
 
+@lru_cache(maxsize=1)
+def _staged_sm86_config() -> tuple[int, int, int] | None:
+    """(block_n, num_warps, num_stages) for the staged prefill kernel on sm_86.
+
+    local-07 (flash-next). The default table gives a staged prefill chunk of
+    256-512 rows BLOCK_N 64 with 2 warps, which runs at less than half the speed
+    of BLOCK_N 32 with 4 warps on sm_86 (FP8 cache, top-k 2048, ~98K context).
+    VLLM_QSA_STAGED_TUNE=0 restores the default; the three
+    VLLM_QSA_STAGED_{BLOCK_N,WARPS,STAGES} variables override single values.
+    """
+    import os
+
+    if current_platform.get_device_capability() != (8, 6):
+        return None
+    if os.environ.get("VLLM_QSA_STAGED_TUNE", "1") == "0":
+        return None
+    return (
+        int(os.environ.get("VLLM_QSA_STAGED_BLOCK_N", "32")),
+        int(os.environ.get("VLLM_QSA_STAGED_WARPS", "4")),
+        int(os.environ.get("VLLM_QSA_STAGED_STAGES", "3")),
+    )
+
+
 # FP8-e4m3 main K/V on sm_86 (flash-next local-02). Upstream reads the cache
 # as float8_e4m3fn and converts it in Triton, which needs the fp8e4nv type that
 # Triton only has on sm_89+. Here every QSA kernel reads the cache as uint8 and
@@ -857,6 +880,11 @@ def qsa_sparse_paged_attention_staged(
     block_n, partial_warps, num_tiles, _ = _select_config(
         num_rows, num_kv_heads, use_prefill_config, selection_width, is_fp8
     )
+    num_stages = 2
+    tuned = _staged_sm86_config()
+    if tuned is not None:
+        block_n, partial_warps, num_stages = tuned
+        num_tiles = triton.cdiv(selection_width, block_n)
 
     if num_buckets == 1:
         acc = max_state = norm_state = q
@@ -918,7 +946,7 @@ def qsa_sparse_paged_attention_staged(
             LAST_BUCKET=bucket == num_buckets - 1,
             IS_FP8=is_fp8,
             num_warps=partial_warps,
-            num_stages=2,
+            num_stages=num_stages,
         )
 
 
